==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Comparateur etalon.png|thumb|Use of a comparator to measure thickness difference between an object and a standard.]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[device]] for [[comparing]] a [[physical]] [[property]] of two objects, or an object with a [[standard]].
# An [[electronic]] device that compares two [[voltage]]s, [[current]]s or [[stream]]s of [[data]].
# {{lb|en|law}} anything that serves [[comparison]]
#* {{quote-book|en|author=European Court of Human Rights|title=McDonald v. The United Kingdom|section=marginal 48|date=20-05-2014|url=http://hudoc.echr.coe.int/eng?i=001-144115|issue=4241/12|passage=The applicant is therefore complaining not of a lack of action but rather of the decision of the local authority to reduce the care package that it had hitherto been making available to her. As such, a more appropriate '''comparator''' would be the case of Watts v. The United Kingdom (dec.), no. 53586/09 of 4 May 2010, in which the Court was content to proceed on the basis that a decision to close the care home where the elderly applicant was resident and to transfer her to another home constituted an interference with her rights under Article 8.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=United States District Court for the District of Connecticut|title=Roxanne Khazarian vs. Gerald Metals, LLC, Metals Trading Corp., Gerald Holdings, LLC, Craig Dean, and Dan Gamez|date=09-11-2017|url=https://ecf.ctd.uscourts.gov/cgi-bin/show_public_doc?2016cv1762-79|issue=No. 3:16-cv-01762(VAB)|passage=Roxanne Khazarian (“Plaintiff”) moved to compel discovery from Gerald Metals, LLC and Metals Trading Corp (“Defendants”), seeking the personnel file of Gary Lerner, an employee of Defendants. […] Defendants object to the production of these documents on the grounds that Mr. Lerner is not an appropriate '''comparator''' for Ms. Khazarian and his personnel file is therefore irrelevant.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} An application or program that [[compare]]s prices, rates, tariffs of flights, smartphones, cars, etc.

